{"id":"NCT06297226","title":"Study of Arlocabtagene Autoleucel (BMS-986393) a GPRC5D-directed CAR T Cell Therapy in Adult Participants With Relapsed or Refractory Multiple Myeloma","official":"A Phase 2, Open-Label, Multicenter Study of Arlocabtagene Autoleucel (BMS-986393), a GPRC5D-directed CAR T Cell Therapy in Adult Participants With Relapsed or Refractory Multiple Myeloma (QUINTESSENTIAL)","summary":"The purpose of this study is to evaluate the effectiveness and safety of Arlocabtagene Autoleucel (BMS-986393) in participants with relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma.","conditions":["Multiple Myeloma"],"interventions":[{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"Arlocabtagene Autoleucel"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria\n\n* Documented diagnosis of multiple myeloma (MM) as per International Myeloma Working Group (IMWG) criteria.\n* Received at least 4 classes of MM treatment \\[including immunomodulatory drug (IMiD), proteasome inhibitor (PI), anti CD38 mAb, anti-BCMA therapy, and at least 3 prior lines of therapy (LOT).\n* Documented disease progression during or after their last anti-myeloma regimen as per IMWG 2016 criteria.\n* Participants must have measurable disease during screening.\n* Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0 or 1.\n\nExclusion Criteria\n\n* Active or history of central nervous system involvement with MM.\n* Active systemic fungal, bacterial, viral, or other infection despite appropriate anti-infective treatment at the time of leukapheresis. Participants with severe infection, severe sepsis or bacteremia in the last 28 days prior to leukapheresis are excluded.\n* Received any prior therapy directed at G protein-coupled receptor class C, group 5, member D (GPRC5D) or has received other prior treatment for MM without the required washout prior to leukapheresis.\n* Other protocol-defined Inclusion/Exclusion criteria apply.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":230,"start":"2024-03-21","pcd":"2026-07-31","upd":"2026-10-06","sponsor":"Juno Therapeutics, Inc., a Bristol-Myers Squibb Company","areas":["oncology"],"central":["BMS Clinical Trials Contact Center www.BMSClinicalTrials.com · 855-907-3286 · Clinical.Trials@bms.com","First line of the email MUST contain NCT # and Site #."],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294-3300","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Susan Bal, Site 0001 · 205-934-1908"},{"f":"Banner MD Anderson Cancer Center","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85234","s":"R","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"Ambuga Badari, Site 0025"},{"f":"University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Sharmilan Thanendrarajan, Site 0037 · 000-000-0000"},{"f":"UCLA Hematology/Oncology - Westwood (Building 200 Suite 214)","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90095","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Sarah Larson, Site 0028 · 310-829-5471"},{"f":"UCSF Helen Diller Medical Center at Parnassus Heights","city":"San Francisco","pr":"California","zip":"94143","s":"R","lat":37.7749,"lon":-122.4194,"c":"Anupama Kumar, Site 0018 · 415-514-0768"},{"f":"Colorado Blood Cancer Institute","city":"Denver","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80218","s":"R","lat":39.7392,"lon":-104.9847,"c":"Tara Gregory, Site 0049 · 720-754-4800"},{"f":"Mayo Clinic in Florida","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32224","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":"Sikander Ailawadhi, Site 0062 · 904-953-0853"},{"f":"Miami Cancer Institute at Baptist Health, Inc.","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33176","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"George Nahas, Site 0045 · 201-310-8558"},{"f":"Moffitt Cancer Center","city":"Tampa","pr":"Florida","zip":"33612","s":"R","lat":27.9475,"lon":-82.4584,"c":"Ciara Freeman, Site 0029 · 813-745-2475"},{"f":"Winship Cancer Institute of Em